From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: AudioReach Secondary TDM support (Lenovo TB321FU speakers)

GUF296's TB321FU-7.1.1 changes to sound/soc/qcom (delta against upstream 7.1.1),
ported onto the 7.2 tree: TDM ports in AudioReach/q6apm-lpass-dais, the
Secondary TDM bit clocks in q6prm, and 8-slot/32-bit TDM setup in the sc8280xp
machine driver. Upstream 7.2 has no TDM support at all, so the AW2308 smart PAs on
SEC_TDM_RX_0 never get a bit clock (no_clks=1, start failed). GUF's TDM startup is
chained in front of the MI2S/SoundWire BE startup.


Rebased onto 7.2.8 for Zaviya: the back-end startup chains to
qcom_snd_sdw_startup, which 7.2.8 uses for these links.

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
index af8736a..08f6441 100644
